  "tagline": "Hadoop's Bigtable clone: strongly consistent wide-column tables on top of HDFS.",
  "description": "HBase is the open-source implementation of Google's Bigtable design for the Hadoop ecosystem: sorted, sparse tables split into regions served by RegionServers, with HDFS for durability and ZooKeeper for coordination. It gives strongly consistent row-level reads and writes over billions of rows and integrates tightly with Spark, MapReduce and Apache Phoenix for SQL. HBase 3.0 shipped in 2026 after a very long development cycle, but momentum has shifted toward cloud-native stores and many large users have migrated away. Choose it today mainly when you already run Hadoop infrastructure.",
